## 7. CONFIGURE A PANEL

Every panel has settings.

IMPORTANT SETTINGS:

Title:
Give the panel a meaningful name.

Description:
Explain what the panel monitors.

Data source:
Select Prometheus.

Query:
Enter your PromQL expression.

Visualization:
Choose Stat, Time series, Gauge, Table, etc.

Unit:
Choose the correct measurement.

Examples:
- CPU = Percent (0-100)
- Memory = Bytes (IEC)
- Network = Bytes/sec
- Pod count = None

Legend:
Choose how metric series are identified.

Thresholds:
Set visual warning levels.

